Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||07-30-2001||03:22 AM||||*sigh*<P>the last 3 hours have really sucked. one of my friends tried to kill himself tonight.<P>he took 26 extra strength tylenols, and refused to go to the hospital... he's there now, 3 hours later, but we're not sure if he's gonna be ok yet....<BR>I don't care if he'll be mad at me for calling 911 and telling them what happened... I just don't want a good friend to die.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||9
Z||000001||Galen||07-30-2001||03:27 AM||||If he's gonna be mad, let em be. a mad friend is better than a dead friend. though a dead friend will be less likely to try to kick your a$$.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"And God said there shall be one in thy owns image, and he made me"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||07-30-2001||03:29 AM||||yeah..<P>I'd never forgive myself if I didn't do anything, so I'm willing to put up with the possibility of him being really pissed off at me..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-30-2001||06:12 AM||||I doubt he'll be pissed off, Steve.  Most attempted suicides are just cries for help.  If he had really wanted to die, he would have done something in private (with no one around to help) or something were there was no turning back (drove his car off a cliff, gunshot to the head, etc).  If he's a really good friend, you need to follow up with this and either try to get him to seek professional help or find professional help for him.  You did the right thing.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jaygee79||07-30-2001||08:48 AM||||When I was in high school I found out that a friend of mine was bulimic .  I told the school nurse about it and she ended up getting her help.  It was supposed to be done anonymously but my friend somehow found out that I was the one who said something.  For the first few months she hated me.  My mother had to pull me out of school for a few days because she was threatning me.  But a few months later she thanked me for it.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooh14.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||07-30-2001||12:07 PM||||well, I went back to the hospital, and his parents were there. I talked with them for a while, and we finally left just after 4am. Seems like he got there just in time, he went home with his parents just after I left.<P>anyway, I'm already 4 hours late for work..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||07-30-2001||01:20 PM||||Steve,<P>You did the right thing, man.<BR>I'm happy that he's okay.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||07-30-2001||02:11 PM||||whenever someone lets you in on something that is 'not right' you then have to decide to either make it right, or to become an accessory.<P>  If you had not called 911 you could end up in prison for assisting a suicide.<P>  Its a commonly held belief that its insane to kill yourself - therefor anyone that is attempting suicide is temporailly crazy - it doenst matter what they want, or what they say - call 911 immediately, sit on them till they arrive if you have to, and let them rant and rave all they want.<P>  If someone is gonna hate me for calling an ambulance then I hope they hate me for a long, long time - for the rest of their life!||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||07-30-2001||02:57 PM||||He'll probably thank you one of these days. If not now, maybe later. Even if he doesn't, you still did the right thing.<P>Considering there are a lot more sure fire ways to commit suicide, this was probably a cry for help... I hope he finds it.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||JSocha||07-30-2001||03:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>If someone is gonna hate me for calling an ambulance <I>then I hope they hate me for a long, long time - for the rest of their life!</I></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>KEN, I'm going to kill myself today...as a friend, please...please...whatever you do, do not call for help or an ambulance!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously, joking aside, you were better off doing what you did DaRkLoRD.  Never feel bad about doing the right thing, especially when it comes to friends.  Don't know what the scoop is with your friend, but he may not think clearly now and may hate you, but later he will when his head is screwed back on right realize that you did right by him.<P>Now Ken, where did you hide my pistola?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||DecadenceR||07-30-2001||03:07 PM||||YOu definitely did the right thing. Like Galen said a mad friend is better than a dead friend.<BR>If more peopl ein this society had your sense of right and wrong, this world would be a much better place. I hope your friend comes out okay.||||reg||1
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||07-30-2001||03:26 PM||||You did the right thing... good job.<P>It's true (seemingly most of the time) that when someone talks about committing suicide, they may or may not be willing to follow through with it, but they *are* asking for help somehow. They are looking for alternatives to killing themselves.<P>The ones who are serious about it, when they make up their mind, just do it without a word. The deed is only found out after the fact by a friend or a loved one.<P>I know this - my oldest brother, Scott - a decorated Viet Nam veteran, who turned to alcohol after post-traumatic stress disorder set in and carved out a permanent niche in his being - put a bullet through his own head without a phone call or a word to anybody... he left the front door to his home propped slightly open and some food for the cats, and a note on the kitchen table leaving everything to our parents, and then killed himself in the bedroom, to be discovered by Dad a day and a half later, when Mom was out of town visiting relatives.<P>(Details included not to be morbid, but to prove that he was relatively lucid when he made up his mind that it was time to go.)<P>You can't stop the ones who are hell-bent for leather on the decision, but you *can* help the ones who make the pronouncement, because they are the ones looking for a reason - *any* reason - to live.||||reg||1
Z||000012||LZeitgeist||07-30-2001||03:31 PM||||JSocha - <P>The words sound funny to you, and that's understandable... but they ring *very* hollow to those who have had to deal with the issue... <P>I'm sure that a lightening of the mood was your full intent, and there are definitely no hard feelings from me, but to a few whose wounds of having to deal with the matter in question are more fresh, the joke may cause more pain than it was worth... :\<P>Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000013||JSocha||07-30-2001||04:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>... but they ring *very* hollow to those who have had to deal with the issue...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have dealt with the issue, more closely then you can ever possibly imagine or experience...as I tried to kill myself back in 1994 by taking 10 bottles of sleeping pills, because all I wanted to do was sleep.  Of course it didn't help as  I was strung out on dope due to the fact that my ex-girlfriends new boyfriend was lacing all my food with everytime he would come over to see her and me and without my knowledge (to both incidents that were going on), so I didn't know if I was coming or going and was haulicinating and/or blacking out.<P>I was pissed at my family (brother, sister-in-law, sister, friends, etc.) for the longest time that called 911 and got me help, because I wanted to sleep, but also by that time I was all messed up in my head.<P>I've also lost a friend to suicide (car in the garage) because she found out she was pregnant and her father was a royal a-hole and abusive.  Some speculation was that it was her fathers which we didn't put past him.<P>Another friend, came close to it and I was the one that had to call his parents to tell them and get him help...at his parents disbelief and denial...but they did just the same, while the rest of the time his and my other buddies wanted to just take him out and party without taking his conversations about it seriously.  That was in '96 as I knew the signs to look for from discussion groups I was in after what I went through.  He still hates me to this day...but that to me is his problem...as I did what I needed to do.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000014||frontal lobe||07-30-2001||04:26 PM||||Well, he SHOULDN'T be mad at you from saving him from an AGONIZING death.<P>Tylenol overdoses kill you by destroying your liver completely.  It is NOT a quick nor painless way to go.<P>DO NOT try to commit suicide with tylenol (do not try to commit suicide).||||reg||1
