Z||000023||Her86GT||07-31-2001||11:26 PM||||Speaking of incidents like this:  I volunteer in trauma emergency here in London and tonight, a guy came in who had tried to shoot himself (up under the chin) but he was unsuccessful at ending his life.  I guess that's a good thing.  The funny thing was is that he called 911 himself - guess he wasn't too serious at ending his life.  We were all happy when he went into the O.R. for plastic surgery.  Just keep on being his friend no matter what and most of these horrible events are just a SERIOUS cry for help.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000024||AusFiero||08-01-2001||06:30 AM||||Thank God you helped him Darklord. Yes he will thank you one day for it. <BR>My best man from my wedding hung himself 2 years ago. I felt ****  about it as I was even going to visit him the night he did. Then didn't.  Always think what if I had. Maybe he would be thanking me too.<P>Just keep an eye on him and let him know you think no worse of him for it. Just tell him to talk if he has too.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
